00:50:52,557 --> 00:50:54,006
-And she moves great.

1281
00:50:54,006 --> 00:50:55,365
-You betcha.

1282
00:50:55,365 --> 00:50:56,744
-We're bald and we're bonding.

1283
00:50:56,744 --> 00:50:59,141
-A question-- where's Jill?

1284
00:50:59,141 --> 00:51:02,838
-She's watching old
movies, Mr. Pattersen.

1285
00:51:02,838 --> 00:51:03,887
-Mr. Pattersen?

1286
00:51:03,887 --> 00:51:06,285
-I'll be right with you.

1287
00:51:06,285 --> 00:51:08,263
-He's a queer duck, eh?

1288
00:51:11,230 --> 00:51:12,070
-Woo.

1289
00:51:12,070 --> 00:51:13,448
Woo.
Woo.

1290
00:51:13,448 --> 00:51:18,933
-I-- uh-- hate to burst
your bubble, but she stinks.

1291
00:51:18,933 --> 00:51:20,842
-No one's allowed backstage.

1292
00:51:20,842 --> 00:51:21,831
-It's Alan Thicke!

1293
00:51:21,831 --> 00:51:22,790
-Oh.

1294
00:51:22,790 --> 00:51:24,249
-Oh-- uh-- Kim.

1295
00:51:24,249 --> 00:51:25,228
-Just enjoy the show.

1296
00:51:28,655 --> 00:51:31,102
-Hi, we're here
to buy everything.

1297
00:51:31,102 --> 00:51:33,750
-Fusion jazz is
for all cultures.

1298
00:51:38,056 --> 00:51:40,514
-Now that's one way to
get service I suppose.

1299
00:51:40,514 --> 00:51:41,813
-Perhaps you can help us.

1300
00:51:41,813 --> 00:51:46,249
-Candy-coated popcorn
peanuts and a prize.

1301
00:51:46,249 --> 00:51:48,227
-We've come to
see Mr. Pattersen.

1302
00:51:48,227 --> 00:51:50,195
-In the office over there.

1303
00:51:50,195 --> 00:51:52,163
-Thank you so much.
-Oh no.

1304
00:51:52,163 --> 00:51:56,120
Thank you.

1305
00:51:56,120 --> 00:51:59,846
-Looks like Clarence
Thomas's wife.

1306
00:51:59,846 --> 00:52:03,133
-It does.

1307
00:52:03,133 --> 00:52:03,783
-Oh, Lee.

1308
00:52:03,783 --> 00:52:04,392
Don't worry.

1309
00:52:04,392 --> 00:52:05,092
She's used to it.

1310
00:52:05,092 --> 00:52:08,209
The Kennedys come here a lot.

1311
00:52:08,209 --> 00:52:10,337
-You'd think with
all the roughnecks

1312
00:52:10,337 --> 00:52:13,454
we get in this place
I'd be used to it.

1313
00:52:13,454 --> 00:52:14,823
-You were right to be afraid.

1314
00:52:14,823 --> 00:52:17,241
-Be very afraid.

1315
00:52:17,241 --> 00:52:19,209
-My, but you are
a sensitive male.

1316
00:52:19,209 --> 00:52:21,547
See you.

1317
00:52:21,547 --> 00:52:24,034
-Oh, it's the other
side of the mountain.

1318
00:52:24,034 --> 00:52:26,172
-What are you doing, Jill?

1319
00:52:26,172 --> 00:52:28,071
-I'm watching you and
mother dance the waltz

1320
00:52:28,071 --> 00:52:29,649
from Lady Be Good.

1321
00:52:29,649 --> 00:52:30,658
-Down in front, old man!

1322
00:52:33,296 --> 00:52:35,564
-Ah, you know, Fred
Astaire and Ginger Rogers.

1323
00:52:35,564 --> 00:52:36,713
Love them.
-Look at that lift.

1324
00:52:36,713 --> 00:52:38,082
Look at the way you moved.

1325
00:52:38,082 --> 00:52:39,301
You were so graceful.

1326
00:52:39,301 --> 00:52:41,029
-Yet so effeminate.

1327
00:52:41,029 --> 00:52:43,217
-I'll just bet you had
Mr. Astaire shaking

1328
00:52:43,217 --> 00:52:45,245
in his dancing pumps.
-I was his dresser actually.

1329
00:52:45,245 --> 00:52:47,363
-I don't think he
was shaking too hard.

1330
00:52:47,363 --> 00:52:49,841
-You think it's kind of sicko
for the leader of a wheelchair

1331
00:52:49,841 --> 00:52:52,698
brigade to get such a charge out
of watching other people dance?

1332
00:52:52,698 --> 00:52:53,368
-Yes, actually.

1333
00:52:53,368 --> 00:52:55,586
-I don't mean the
way my sister dances.

1334
00:52:55,586 --> 00:52:56,665
That's not dancing.

1335
00:52:56,665 --> 00:52:57,354
-It's typing.

1336
00:52:57,354 --> 00:52:59,282
-That's aerobics.

1337
00:52:59,282 --> 00:53:01,670
Now what you did was dancing.

1338
00:53:01,670 --> 00:53:04,578
Bet you could still do it, too.
If you really wanted to.

1339
00:53:04,578 --> 00:53:06,866
-Maybe if I had a hip.

1340
00:53:06,866 --> 00:53:07,995
-You're right, dad.

1341
00:53:07,995 --> 00:53:11,841
With some hot towels on my
legs at half hourly intervals,

1342
00:53:11,841 --> 00:53:12,860
couple of FDR canes.
-Oh, yes.

1343
00:53:12,860 --> 00:53:13,360
Oh, yeah.

1344
00:53:13,360 --> 00:53:15,937
-I might be able to
manage a couple of steps.

1345
00:53:15,937 --> 00:53:19,584
-A cane didn't hurt
Mr. Astaire's career.

1346
00:53:19,584 --> 00:53:20,403
-Oh, bite me.

1347
00:53:20,403 --> 00:53:22,821
-Don't you just hate
dealing with it?

1348
00:53:22,821 --> 00:53:25,928
An ex-hoofer with two
daughters, one wheels,

1349
00:53:25,928 --> 00:53:27,457
the other cartwheels.

1350
00:53:27,457 --> 00:53:32,043
-One is shy and retiring, and--
uh-- one has a smart mouth.

1351
00:53:32,043 --> 00:53:32,572
-Ooh, touche.

1352
00:53:32,572 --> 00:53:35,040
-My sister, shy and retiring?

1353
00:53:35,040 --> 00:53:36,868
The decade's answer
to Isadora Duncan?

1354
00:53:36,868 --> 00:53:37,368
-What?

1355
00:53:37,368 --> 00:53:38,107
She wears scarves?

1356
00:53:40,705 --> 00:53:41,764
-That's angry Jill.

1357
00:53:41,764 --> 00:53:43,342
-Sorry.
I'm bitter.

1358
00:53:43,342 --> 00:53:45,301
-I wonder what she calls me.

1359
00:53:45,301 --> 00:53:46,080
-Gimped?

1360
00:53:46,080 --> 00:53:47,029
-Oh, that's mean.

1361
00:53:47,029 --> 00:53:48,208
-Isn't that what
you call yourself?

1362
00:53:48,208 --> 00:53:49,517
-Hey, now.
Wait a minute.

1363
00:53:49,517 --> 00:53:51,785
I took two steps yesterday.
-Time to go, honey.

1364
00:53:51,785 --> 00:53:52,604
-I know.

1365
00:53:52,604 --> 00:53:53,453
-Oh.

1366
00:53:53,453 --> 00:53:55,212
This is my favorite part.

1367
00:53:55,212 --> 00:53:57,490
This is your audition
for the dancing pirate.

1368
00:53:57,490 --> 00:53:58,938
This-- this is a blast.

1369
00:53:58,938 --> 00:54:00,447
-You were really gadding it up.

1370
00:54:00,447 --> 00:54:04,204
-We'd like to buy

1371
00:54:06,831 --> 00:54:08,729
-Mr. Pattersen, how
good to meet you

1372
00:54:08,729 --> 00:54:11,537
in person after all
those phone calls.

1373
00:54:11,537 --> 00:54:14,564
I'm Jonathan Chan,
and this is Mr. Lika.

1374
00:54:14,564 --> 00:54:16,962
-Uh-- are you related
to Mr. Phlegm.

1375
00:54:16,962 --> 00:54:18,211
-Would you excuse
us, young lady?

1376
00:54:18,211 --> 00:54:22,277
Your father and I have some
important business to discuss.

1377
00:54:22,277 --> 00:54:23,776
-In a pig's eye.

1378
00:54:23,776 --> 00:54:25,304
-Jill, come on.

1379
00:54:25,304 --> 00:54:27,852
-One pigs, one sweats.
-Watch your feet, gentlemen.

1380
00:54:27,852 --> 00:54:31,019
I'm lethal with this thing.
You mind?

1381
00:54:33,827 --> 00:54:35,016
-Ooh, my foot.

1382
00:54:35,016 --> 00:54:36,694
Oof.

1383
00:54:36,694 --> 00:54:39,811
-So let's talk business.

1384
00:54:39,811 --> 00:54:41,560
-There's a little
trouble up front.

1385
00:54:41,560 --> 00:54:42,539
-Big China.

1386
00:54:42,539 --> 00:54:43,768
-While Attila the
Hun was distracted,

1387
00:54:43,768 --> 00:54:45,656
I saw my chance
to get backstage.

1388
00:54:45,656 --> 00:54:47,694
This was gonna be easy.

1389
00:54:47,694 --> 00:54:49,872
-At first.
-Oops.

1390
00:54:49,872 --> 00:54:52,330
[CHATTERING]

1391
00:54:55,267 --> 00:54:58,215
-Hey, can I get
my pencil in here?

1392
00:54:58,215 --> 00:55:01,462
OK, give me the number.

1393
00:55:01,462 --> 00:55:02,311
OK.

1394
00:55:02,311 --> 00:55:06,417
-Thank god I lost my
peripheral vision in the war.

1395
00:55:06,417 --> 00:55:09,774
-Hey, what is this? "Dream
On" all of a sudden?

1396
00:55:09,774 --> 00:55:11,393
-Hey.

1397
00:55:11,393 --> 00:55:12,851
Don't take your
hand from your eyes

1398
00:55:12,851 --> 00:55:13,920
you're gonna walk into the wall.

1399
00:55:13,920 --> 00:55:16,158
-You got a D cup
or it's a-- decaf.

1400
00:55:16,158 --> 00:55:17,497
Decaf.

1401
00:55:17,497 --> 00:55:18,766
-You really shouldn't
be back here.

1402
00:55:18,766 --> 00:55:20,754
Our bouncer has a small
personality problem.

1403
00:55:20,754 --> 00:55:21,254
-Who?

1404
00:55:21,254 --> 00:55:22,133
Attila the Hun?

1405
00:55:22,133 --> 00:55:24,171
We're pals.

1406
00:55:24,171 --> 00:55:26,049
-Kelly Pattersen,
I'm Max Keller.

1407
00:55:26,049 --> 00:55:27,638
Looking for a girl.

1408
00:55:27,638 --> 00:55:28,157
-New or used.

1409
00:55:28,157 --> 00:55:30,605
-If the stars are in the
right places it'd be you.

1410
00:55:30,605 --> 00:55:31,315
The name's Terry.

1411
00:55:31,315 --> 00:55:32,384
You know her?

1412
00:55:32,384 --> 00:55:34,951
-Uh-- no dancer
here named Carrie.

1413
00:55:34,951 --> 00:55:35,451
Look.

1414
00:55:35,451 --> 00:55:37,429
We're on a break now, and
I've gotta go meet someone.

1415
00:55:37,429 --> 00:55:39,317
Sorry.
-Yeah, but I--

1416
00:55:39,317 --> 00:55:41,176
-Sorry.

1417
00:55:41,176 --> 00:55:42,934
-Just take a look at
this picture and see if--

1418
00:55:42,934 --> 00:55:44,473
-Is it my breath?

1419
00:55:44,473 --> 00:55:47,310
-Wasn't as easy as I thought.

1420
00:55:47,310 --> 00:55:48,769
-And it's time for
the bouncer to get

1421
00:55:48,769 --> 00:55:49,658
into his spandex leotard.

1422
00:55:54,583 --> 00:55:56,282
-Mwah!

1423
00:55:56,282 --> 00:55:59,119
-Kelly did mention a small
personality problem of yours.

1424
00:55:59,119 --> 00:56:00,508
-Yeah, you hate Van Pattens.

1425
00:56:03,925 --> 00:56:06,163
-It's the Battle of
the Network Has-beens!

1426
00:56:06,163 --> 00:56:09,430
-Woo.

1427
00:56:09,430 --> 00:56:11,268
-Yeah, that's for all of that
Patten getting kicked out

1428
00:56:11,268 --> 00:56:13,766
of bars.
-How do you like this, pal?

1429
00:56:13,766 --> 00:56:16,534
Here's a little warning.
-Uh-oh.

1430
00:56:16,534 --> 00:56:18,052
Seven years bad acting.

1431
00:56:18,052 --> 00:56:18,732
-Need more practice.

1432
00:56:22,268 --> 00:56:24,306
-I told you eight is enough!

1433
00:56:24,306 --> 00:56:25,755
-So seven years bad luck.

1434
00:56:28,483 --> 00:56:29,881
Meanwhile, the
master was getting us

1435
00:56:29,881 --> 00:56:30,831
into even more trouble.

1436
00:56:30,831 --> 00:56:34,247
-Snapping off car antennas
in the parking lot.

1437
00:56:34,247 --> 00:56:37,205
-You ninja masters
blend in so well.

1438
00:56:37,205 --> 00:56:37,704
-Hm.

1439
00:56:37,704 --> 00:56:39,133
Especially in discos.

1440
00:56:39,133 --> 00:56:42,550
-Like the roots of a great
oak, we take hold where we can.

1441
00:56:42,550 --> 00:56:46,756
-The only protection I need
is from people like you.

1442
00:56:46,756 --> 00:56:49,414
Now get out.

1443
00:56:49,414 --> 00:56:52,591
-Isn't everyone
here really phony?

1444
00:56:52,591 --> 00:56:53,450
-I cannot move.

1445
00:56:56,228 --> 00:56:59,325
-That's an unusual
insignia on your ring.

1446
00:56:59,325 --> 00:57:02,911
-An ancient household
going back for centuries.

1447
00:57:02,911 --> 00:57:07,607
-Knights of Columbus?
-Yes, I know.

1448
00:57:07,607 --> 00:57:09,386
-You and I and Butterflyman?

1449
00:57:09,386 --> 00:57:10,485
-We've been told to leave.

1450
00:57:10,485 --> 00:57:11,254
Let's go.

1451
00:57:11,254 --> 00:57:11,933
-Come on, man.

1452
00:57:11,933 --> 00:57:13,892
That Jack Perkins
guy really scares me.

1453
00:57:13,892 --> 00:57:17,488
-I may leave when he lets me go.

1454
00:57:17,488 --> 00:57:20,925
-Tonight on Ninja Master,
Lee Van Cleef and Sho Koshugi

1455
00:57:20,925 --> 00:57:22,793
in a deadly game
of cat and mouse.

1456
00:57:25,661 --> 00:57:27,629
-The old man hired you.

1457
00:57:27,629 --> 00:57:29,148
-I am not for hire.

1458
00:57:29,148 --> 00:57:33,534
-We are all for
hire in dark times.

1459
00:57:33,534 --> 00:57:34,503
-The dark times have gone.

1460
00:57:34,503 --> 00:57:36,581
-Are you guys speaking
in haiku all of a sudden?

1461
00:57:36,581 --> 00:57:37,080
Whoa.

1462
00:57:37,080 --> 00:57:42,146
-Night is always
with us, master.

1463
00:57:42,146 --> 00:57:43,704
-Could we get to the point?
Geez, what a drip.

1464
00:57:47,891 --> 00:57:50,119
-What? she's giving
herself her autograph?

1465
00:57:54,355 --> 00:57:55,774
-Taking her own order.

1466
00:57:55,774 --> 00:57:57,842
-Here's her last address.

1467
00:57:57,842 --> 00:57:59,200
-Oh.

1468
00:57:59,200 --> 00:58:01,269
Oh, he's so adorable.

1469
00:58:01,269 --> 00:58:02,957
-Spooky chick.

1470
00:58:02,957 --> 00:58:05,725
-One glimpse of those blue eyes,
and every girl falls for him.

1471
00:58:05,725 --> 00:58:08,002
I've gotta learn his technique.

1472
00:58:08,002 --> 00:58:09,821
So when's the last
time you saw Terry?

1473
00:58:09,821 --> 00:58:10,580
-Terry Thomas?

1474
00:58:10,580 --> 00:58:13,208
-About a week ago.
Look.

1475
00:58:13,208 --> 00:58:14,776
I hope your friend isn't
it expecting to find--

1476
00:58:14,776 --> 00:58:15,935
-No!

1477
00:58:15,935 --> 00:58:17,704
-She's really messed up.

1478
00:58:17,704 --> 00:58:18,483
Drugs.

1479
00:58:18,483 --> 00:58:21,460
-Yeah, she ran out.

1480
00:58:21,460 --> 00:58:24,717
-So how'd you get
past good old Attila?

1481
00:58:24,717 --> 00:58:28,184
-He carries some cute little
tricks around with him.

1482
00:58:28,184 --> 00:58:28,824
Like this.

1483
00:58:28,824 --> 00:58:30,032
-Oh, that's the
blade from my mixer.

1484
00:58:32,940 --> 00:58:35,018
-He's just leaving.
-Here's your gerbil.

1485
00:58:35,018 --> 00:58:38,185
-Daylight already.

1486
00:58:38,185 --> 00:58:41,752
I didn't realize we
were in there so long.

1487
00:58:41,752 --> 00:58:44,929
-Hey-- hey, that's Nancy Kulp
Nancy Kulp just walked by!

1488
00:58:44,929 --> 00:58:46,208
-What the hell was
that all about?

1489
00:58:46,208 --> 00:58:47,776
-This is not a toy.

1490
00:58:47,776 --> 00:58:50,694
You only throw a shuriken
against another human being

1491
00:58:50,694 --> 00:58:51,983
in self-defense.

1492
00:58:51,983 --> 00:58:54,520
You ever again take another
weapon out of my case,

1493
00:58:54,520 --> 00:58:57,138
you be prepared to use
it against your enemy,

1494
00:58:57,138 --> 00:58:58,447
even if it's me.

1495
00:58:58,447 --> 00:59:00,175
-And stop using my toothbrush.

1496
00:59:00,175 --> 00:59:01,904
-I'd rather not.

1497
00:59:01,904 --> 00:59:03,182
-Not yet anyway.

1498
00:59:03,182 --> 00:59:06,080
-I guess you don't respect
what you don't understand.

1499
00:59:06,080 --> 00:59:07,788
-I don't respect why
this movie was made.

1500
00:59:07,788 --> 00:59:09,327
-Amen.

1501
00:59:09,327 --> 00:59:10,785
-Kelly's address
and phone number.

1502
00:59:10,785 --> 00:59:11,904
-All right.

1503
00:59:11,904 --> 00:59:13,173
-I managed to get
that much before you

1504
00:59:13,173 --> 00:59:14,602
hauled me out of there.

1505
00:59:14,602 --> 00:59:16,310
The other address
is your daughter's.

1506
00:59:16,310 --> 00:59:17,649
-Kelly knows her?

1507
00:59:17,649 --> 00:59:19,158
-She knows a girl
named Terry, who

1508
00:59:19,158 --> 00:59:20,517
used to be a dancer and a pilot.

1509
00:59:20,517 --> 00:59:21,855
-Terry &amp; the Pilots!

1510
00:59:21,855 --> 00:59:24,123
-It doesn't necessarily
mean she's your daughter.

1511
00:59:24,123 --> 00:59:26,541
-Let's find out.

1512
00:59:26,541 --> 00:59:27,810
-I'll do the driving.

1513
00:59:27,810 --> 00:59:29,299
You fill the [INAUDIBLE]
with shurikens.

1514
00:59:29,299 --> 00:59:29,798
-What?

1515
00:59:29,798 --> 00:59:31,057
You wanna translate
that for us, Tim?

1516
00:59:33,994 --> 00:59:35,683
-Get a windsock for the
microphone next time

1517
00:59:35,683 --> 00:59:36,952
you do an outdoor scene.

1518
00:59:36,952 --> 00:59:38,790
Come on!
-I don't understand.

1519
00:59:38,790 --> 00:59:40,638
-They're leaving now.
-I know.

1520
00:59:40,638 --> 00:59:41,568
I'm sitting next to you.

1521
00:59:41,568 --> 00:59:44,065
-Now comes the fun part--
riding with a ninja.

1522
00:59:44,065 --> 00:59:47,852
-We'll be the judge of that.

1523
00:59:47,852 --> 00:59:51,648
-Chevy van, a good,
modern production.

1524
00:59:51,648 --> 00:59:52,717
-We're being followed.

1525
00:59:52,717 --> 00:59:53,677
-Of course, we are.

1526
00:59:53,677 --> 00:59:57,663
We're in an action-packed
made for TV movie.

1527
00:59:57,663 --> 00:59:58,163
-Quick.

1528
00:59:58,163 --> 01:00:00,021
Take a turn here on
Steven J Canal Boulevard!

1529
01:00:08,313 --> 01:00:09,282
-Well, here's a surprise.

1530
